                    "href": "https://api.github.com/repos/cython/cython/pulls/comments/4437223652"
                }
            },
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This could be spelled generically with a slice assignment:\n```suggestion\n            args[arg_index:arg_index+1] = [int_node]\n```\nBut I'm not sure it's any better. Doesn't seem more clear, at least. But it also took me a moment to understand the two if-cases and why they do what they do. It's only clear from the initial method comment, which doesn't entirely cover the following lines.\nMaybe add a comment:\n```suggestion\n            # Replace None by default value, or append the default.\n            if len(args) == arg_index:\n                args.append(int_node)\n            else:\n                args[arg_index] = int_node\n```\nOr maybe give the two initial (`or `-ed) conditions different variable names, like `argument_is_missing` and `argument_is_none`. Or just `argument_is_missing` for the len-based one?",
            "commit_id": "77de113b142649ca6111b67192154b3e4b0668d7",
            "copilot_code_review_sources": [],
            "created_at": "2026-11-01T20:31:17Z",
            "diff_hunk": "@@ -4366,7 +4366,10 @@ def _inject_int_default_argument(self, node, args, arg_index, type, default_valu\n                 int_node = ExprNodes.IntNode.for_int(node.pos, int(default_value))\n             else:\n                 int_node = ExprNodes.IntNode(node.pos, value=str(default_value), type=type)\n-            args.append(int_node)\n+            if len(args) == arg_index:\n+                args.append(int_node)\n+            else:\n+                args[arg_index] = int_node",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/cython/cython/pull/8100#discussion_r4437223652",
